{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-39401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-39401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}}-\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}=-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}}+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}=-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-39401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d64544b8d6c0e1cc4c0520b9a8a5f2d91b05c88570013da0af1e57fb9885897"} {"question" "q-39401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-39401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{13}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-39401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-40402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{2}}{4}$, where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{6} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{6} \\\\ \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-40402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =x\\cdot {q}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{6} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{6} \\\\ \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}+3\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}_{2}}{4}=\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{4}=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-40402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d64544b8d6c0e1cc4c0520b9a8a5f2d91b05c88570013da0af1e57fb9885897"} {"question" "q-40402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-40402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "6\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-40402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-81105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $10{x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-81105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{2}}{{q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot (-1)}{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15+3}{9+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n10{x}_{2}=10\\cdot \\frac{9}{5}=18.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-81105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d64544b8d6c0e1cc4c0520b9a8a5f2d91b05c88570013da0af1e57fb9885897"} {"question" "q-81105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-81105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "18"] ["math" "27"] ["math" "9"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-81105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-81137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $30{x}_{1},$ where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-81137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3+4}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n30{x}_{1}=30\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}=6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-81137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0d64544b8d6c0e1cc4c0520b9a8a5f2d91b05c88570013da0af1e57fb9885897"} {"question" "q-81137" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-81137" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-81137" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-102341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $4{x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069683/state.json" "file_sha256" "48f1f7ace2c7c5bfda9716bfa5f28fe266b16c3bfcd60ae4ac9842ccb1fd5a09"} {"question" "q-102341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{2}}{{q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\cdot (-5)+(-12)\\cdot 4}{(-5)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-75-48}{25+16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{123}{41} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n4{x}_{1}=4\\cdot (-3)=-12.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capt